module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.EffectiveCartier
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SheafRankOne.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ConormalAffineCotangent.Sections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.CartierComplementDense.Basic
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# The affine-local nonzerodivisor description of an effective Cartier divisor

Let `X` be a scheme and `I : X.IdealSheafData` a closed subscheme whose ideal sheaf is an
invertible `𝒪_X`-module, that is, an effective Cartier divisor in the sense of
`Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor`. This file proves the forward direction of
[Stacks, Tag 01WS]: around every point of `X` there is an affine open `V` and an element
`f ∈ Γ(X, V)` which is a nonzerodivisor and generates `I.ideal V`.

Nothing new is proved about sheaves here. Three results of the library are composed:

* `Stacks.SheafRankOne.exists_cover_trivialization_of_isInvertible` — clause 2 of
  [Stacks, Tag 0B8M] in sectionwise form — produces an open cover of `X` and, over each
  member `V`, a restriction-compatible family of `Γ(X, W)`-linear isomorphisms
  `ℐ(W) ≃ Γ(X, W)` for every open `W ≤ V`;
* `Stacks.SheafDescent.Trivialization.eq_smul_basisAt` says every section of `ℐ` over `W` is
  the local basis element scaled by its image under that isomorphism;
* `Stacks.Conormal.AffineCotangent.Sections.exists_idealSheaf_section_iff_mem_ker` together
  with Mathlib's `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_subschemeι_app` says that the
  sections of `ℐ` over an affine open `V` are exactly `I.ideal V`, read inside `Γ(X, V)`
  through the inclusion `ℐ ⟶ 𝒪_X`.

The generator is the image of the local basis element, and both of its properties are the
same two-line computation: `ι m = θ m * ι b` for every section `m`, which makes the image of
`ι` the ideal generated by `f = ι b`, and which makes `a * f = 0` force `a = 0` because `ι` is
injective and `θ (a • b) = a`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.CartierAffineLocal.exists_affineOpen_nonZeroDivisor`: **the forward direction of
  [Stacks, Tag 01WS]**. Around every point of `X` the divisor is cut out on an affine open by
  a single nonzerodivisor. `exists_affineOpen_isRegular` is the same statement in the `IsRegular`
  spelling of the tagged statement.
* `Stacks.CartierAffineLocal.isLocallyPrincipal`: the remark following Definition 01WR, that
  an effective Cartier divisor is locally principal.
* `Stacks.CartierAffineLocal.isSchemeTheoreticallyDense_supportCompl`: the density half of
  [Stacks, Tag 07ZU] **unconditionally**. It comes from
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CartierComplementDense`
  `.isSchemeTheoreticallyDense_supportCompl_of_nonZeroDivisor`, which until now carried the
  affine-local description as a hypothesis.

## Implementation notes

**Three definitionally equal but syntactically distinct spellings of `Γ(X, W)` meet at the key
step, and instance search crosses none of them.** The inclusion `ℐ ⟶ 𝒪_X` is `kernel.ι` of a
morphism of `SheafOfModules (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace)`, so its
component over `W` is linear over
`(structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace).val.obj (op W)` and lands in
`(SheafOfModules.unit _).val.obj (op W)`; the trivialization's `θ` is linear over
`(Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureRingPresheaf X.toRingedSpace.presheaf).obj
  (op W)`; and the ideal
`I.ideal ⟨W, hW⟩` and the nonzerodivisor condition live in `Γ(X, W)`. Writing `map_smul` or
`smul_eq_mul` directly fails with `failed to synthesize instance of type class HSMul ...`,
because instance synthesis runs at a reducibility setting that does not unfold the `def`s
`structureSheafRing`, `CategoryTheory.sheafCompose` and
`CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.unit`.

**The fix is to carry the module structures inside the argument types**, as
`Stacks.DenominatorIdealInvertible.injective_unitApp_of_linearEquiv` does: the section `Core`
below is stated for a bare `Semiring R` and a bare `Module R M`, with the module structure an
*implicit* argument rather than an instance to be found, and with `θ : M ≃ₗ[R] R` and
`ι : M →ₗ[R] R` as explicit arguments. At the application site `R`, `M` and the module
structure are fixed by unification against `θ`'s type, and `ι`'s type is then checked by
`isDefEq` at *default* transparency — which does unfold those `def`s. So the crossing is paid
once, by the application, and `map_smul` and `smul_eq_mul` inside the helpers are elaborated
in a context where only one spelling exists.

**The conclusions are stated so that no `•` on a section of `ℐ` ever appears outside `Core`.**
`apply_eq_mul` and `exists_apply_eq_mul` conclude equations between elements of `R` alone, and
`eq_zero_of_mul_eq_zero` takes and returns only elements of `R`, so the commutative-algebra
step `eq_span_singleton_of_exists` needs no module theory at all and runs at the `Γ(X, V)`
spelling. This is also why `θ.symm` is applied to a ring element rather than `•` being used to
produce a section: a term-level coercion of `a : Γ(X, V)` into `θ`'s scalar ring is a defeq
check, whereas `a • b` would be an instance search.

## What is not done, and what is not claimed

**No `@[stacks 01WS]` attribute is attached.** Tag 01WS is an `iff`, and only the forward
direction is proved here. Nothing below bears on the reverse direction — a closed subscheme
locally cut out by a nonzerodivisor has invertible ideal sheaf.

**The reverse direction has a known route.** From `I.ideal V = Ideal.span {f}` with `f` regular
one gets an isomorphism `ℐ|_V ≅ 𝒪|_V` of modules on the over-site, hence that `ℐ` is finite
locally free of rank one, hence invertible by
`Stacks.SheafDescent.isInvertible_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one`, or directly from a family
of isomorphisms through `Trivialization.ofIso` and `isInvertible_of_trivialization`. The step
from the chart-local isomorphisms to local freeness moves a module sheaf along `Scheme.Opens.ι`
(`M.over V`); doing it without `set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false` needs the
bijection route of `Stacks.NormMapInvertible.bijective_smul_restrictAppIso`. That is not done
here.

Tag 01WS is also stated in [Stacks] with an explicit isomorphism
`D ×_X V ≅ Spec (Γ(X, V) / (f))` compatible with the closed immersions. That packaging is not
produced here; `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeIsoSpecQuotient` is the
Mathlib input it would be assembled from. The ideal-level statement is the one the consumers
in this repository ask for.

Both directions of 01WS pass through "an invertible sheaf of modules is locally free of rank
one". That descent step is proved, as
`Stacks.SheafRankOne.exists_cover_trivialization_of_isInvertible` and
`Stacks.SheafRankOne.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one_of_isInvertible_scheme`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07ZU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07ZU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B8M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B8M)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace Opposite
open RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction

universe u

namespace Stacks.CartierAffineLocal

/-! ### The typeclass-free core

Every statement in this section carries its module structure inside the types of its explicit
arguments: `inst` is an implicit argument, not an instance to be synthesized, and `R` and `M`
are determined by unification against `θ`. See the module docstring. -/

section Core

variable {R : Type u} [Semiring R] {M : Type u} [AddCommMonoid M] {inst : Module R M}

/-- **The arithmetic of a rank-one trivialization.** If every element of `M` is the local basis
element `b` scaled by its image under `θ`, then every value of a linear map `ι : M ⟶ R` is a
multiple of `ι b`, with the explicit coefficient `θ m`. -/
theorem apply_eq_mul (θ : M ≃ₗ[R] R) (ι : M →ₗ[R] R) (b : M)
    (hb : ∀ m : M, m = θ m • b) (m : M) : ι m = θ m * ι b := by
  conv_lhs => rw [hb m]
  rw [map_smul, smul_eq_mul]

/-- **Every multiple of `ι b` is a value of `ι`.** The witness is `θ.symm a`, so no scalar
action on `M` has to be formed at the application site. -/
theorem exists_apply_eq_mul (θ : M ≃ₗ[R] R) (ι : M →ₗ[R] R) (b : M)
    (hb : ∀ m : M, m = θ m • b) (a : R) : ι (θ.symm a) = a * ι b := by
  rw [apply_eq_mul θ ι b hb, θ.apply_symm_apply]

/-- **The image of the local basis element is a nonzerodivisor.** If `a * ι b = 0` then
`ι (a • b) = 0`, so `a • b = 0` because `ι` is injective, and applying `θ` gives `a = 0`. -/
theorem eq_zero_of_mul_eq_zero (θ : M ≃ₗ[R] R) (ι : M →ₗ[R] R)
    (hι : Function.Injective ι) (b : M) (hθb : θ b = 1)
    (a : R) (h : a * ι b = 0) : a = 0 := by
  have h1 : ι (a • b) = 0 := by rw [map_smul, smul_eq_mul, h]
  have h2 : a • b = 0 := hι (by rw [h1, map_zero])
  have h3 : θ (a • b) = 0 := by rw [h2, map_zero]
  rwa [map_smul, hθb, smul_eq_mul, mul_one] at h3

end Core

/-! ### Commutative algebra

An ideal whose elements are exactly the multiples of one of its elements is generated by it.
Separated out so that no module appears at the `Γ(X, V)` spelling. -/

/-- An ideal is generated by `f` as soon as its elements are exactly the multiples of `f`. -/
theorem eq_span_singleton_of_exists {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (J : Ideal R) (f : R)
    (h : ∀ r : R, r ∈ J ↔ ∃ a : R, r = a * f) : J = Ideal.span {f} := by
  have hfJ : f ∈ J := (h f).2 ⟨1, (one_mul f).symm⟩
  refine le_antisymm (fun r hr => ?_) ?_
  · obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := (h r).1 hr
    exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mpr ⟨a, rfl⟩
  · rwa [Ideal.span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff]

/-! ### The ideal sheaf and its sections -/

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)

/-- The inclusion of the ideal sheaf into the structure sheaf, namely `kernel.ι`. -/
abbrev incl :
    Stacks.ClosedImmersion.idealSheaf I.subschemeι.toLRSHom.toShHom ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace) :=
  kernel.ι (SheafOfModules.unitToPushforwardObjUnit
    (structureSheafHom I.subschemeι.toLRSHom.toShHom))

/-- **Over an affine open the sections of the ideal sheaf are `I.ideal V`.** A section of
`𝒪_X` over an affine open `V` lies in `I.ideal V` exactly when it is the image of a section of
the ideal sheaf. This is
`Stacks.Conormal.AffineCotangent.Sections.exists_idealSheaf_section_iff_mem_ker` composed with
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_subschemeι_app`. -/
theorem mem_ideal_iff_exists (V : X.affineOpens) (r : Γ(X, V.1)) :
    r ∈ I.ideal V ↔
      ∃ y : (Stacks.ClosedImmersion.idealSheaf I.subschemeι.toLRSHom.toShHom).val.obj (op V.1),
        (incl I).val.app (op V.1) y = r := by
  rw [← I.ker_subschemeι_app V]
  exact (Stacks.Conormal.AffineCotangent.Sections.exists_idealSheaf_section_iff_mem_ker
    I.subschemeι V.1 r).symm

/-- A section of the ideal sheaf is determined by its image in the structure sheaf: the
inclusion is a monomorphism. This is
`Stacks.Conormal.Locality.idealSheaf_section_injective` at `I.subschemeι`. -/
theorem injective_incl_app (W : X.Opens) :
    Function.Injective ((incl I).val.app (op W)).hom :=
  Stacks.Conormal.Locality.idealSheaf_section_injective I.subschemeι W

/-! ### The forward direction of Tag 01WS -/

/-- **Every point of a scheme has an affine open neighbourhood inside a given open.** The
affine opens form a basis of the topology. -/
@[ega "I 2.1.3"]
theorem exists_affineOpens_le {x : X} (U : X.Opens) (hx : x ∈ U) :
    ∃ V : X.affineOpens, x ∈ (V : Set X) ∧ (V : X.Opens) ≤ U := by
  obtain ⟨-, ⟨W, hW, rfl⟩, hxW, hWU⟩ :=
    X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open hx U.2
  exact ⟨⟨W, hW⟩, hxW, hWU⟩

/-- **The generator, on an affine open carrying a trivialization.** If the ideal sheaf is
sectionwise trivial over an open `U` and `V ≤ U` is affine, then `I.ideal V` is generated by
the image `f` of the local basis element, and `f` is a nonzerodivisor.

Both halves are the single computation `ι m = θ m * f` of `apply_eq_mul`: it makes every
element of `I.ideal V` a multiple of `f`, and together with injectivity of `ι` it makes
`a * f = 0` force `a = 0`. -/
theorem exists_nonZeroDivisor_of_trivialization {U : X.Opens}
    (t : Stacks.SheafDescent.Trivialization X.toRingedSpace.presheaf
      (Stacks.ClosedImmersion.idealSheaf I.subschemeι.toLRSHom.toShHom).val U)
    (V : X.affineOpens) (h : (V : X.Opens) ⟶ U) :
    ∃ f : Γ(X, V.1), f ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, V.1) ∧ I.ideal V = Ideal.span {f} := by
  -- The three spellings of `Γ(X, V)` are crossed exactly here, by these two applications.
  have hmul := apply_eq_mul (t.θ (V : X.Opens) h) ((incl I).val.app (op V.1)).hom
    (t.basisAt h) (fun m => t.eq_smul_basisAt h m)
  have hex := exists_apply_eq_mul (t.θ (V : X.Opens) h) ((incl I).val.app (op V.1)).hom
    (t.basisAt h) (fun m => t.eq_smul_basisAt h m)
  have hnzd := eq_zero_of_mul_eq_zero (t.θ (V : X.Opens) h) ((incl I).val.app (op V.1)).hom
    (injective_incl_app I V.1) (t.basisAt h) (t.θ_basisAt h)
  refine ⟨(incl I).val.app (op V.1) (t.basisAt h), ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_right.mpr hnzd
  · refine eq_span_singleton_of_exists _ _ fun r => ?_
    rw [mem_ideal_iff_exists]
    exact ⟨fun ⟨y, hy⟩ => ⟨_, hy ▸ hmul y⟩, fun ⟨a, ha⟩ => ⟨_, (hex a).trans ha.symm⟩⟩

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 01WS, forward direction.** An effective Cartier divisor is, around
every point of the ambient scheme, cut out on an affine open neighbourhood by a single
nonzerodivisor.

The quantifier is over all of `X` rather than over the support of `I`: on an affine open
disjoint from the support the ideal is the unit ideal, which is generated by the
nonzerodivisor `1`, and the trivializing cover supplied by
`Stacks.SheafRankOne.exists_cover_trivialization_of_isInvertible` covers `X`, so no case
distinction is needed.

No `@[stacks 01WS]` attribute is attached: the tag is an `iff` and the reverse direction is
not proved. See the module docstring. -/
@[ega "IV 21.2.7" "Forward implication"]
theorem exists_affineOpen_nonZeroDivisor
    (hI : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor I) (x : X) :
    ∃ V : X.affineOpens, x ∈ (V : Set X) ∧ ∃ f : Γ(X, V.1),
      f ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, V.1) ∧ I.ideal V = Ideal.span {f} := by
  have hinv : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.toRingedSpace.presheaf
      (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace).property
        (Stacks.ClosedImmersion.idealSheaf I.subschemeι.toLRSHom.toShHom) := hI
  obtain ⟨U, hU, t⟩ := Stacks.SheafRankOne.exists_cover_trivialization_of_isInvertible
    (X := X.toRingedSpace) (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace).property
      (Stacks.ClosedImmersion.idealSheaf I.subschemeι.toLRSHom.toShHom)
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := Opens.mem_iSup.mp (hU ▸ Opens.mem_top x)
  obtain ⟨V, hxV, hVU⟩ := exists_affineOpens_le (x := x) (U y) hy
  exact ⟨V, hxV, exists_nonZeroDivisor_of_trivialization I (t y).some V (homOfLE hVU)⟩

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 01WS, forward direction, in the `IsRegular` spelling.** The
generator is a regular element of `Γ(X, V)`; `isRegular_iff_mem_nonZeroDivisors` is the bridge.
Stated because the statement of Tag 01WS phrases the conclusion with `IsRegular`, so this makes
the faithfulness of `exists_affineOpen_nonZeroDivisor` visible. -/
theorem exists_affineOpen_isRegular
    (hI : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor I) (x : X) :
    ∃ V : X.affineOpens, x ∈ (V : Set X) ∧ ∃ f : Γ(X, V.1),
      IsRegular f ∧ I.ideal V = Ideal.span {f} := by
  obtain ⟨V, hxV, f, hf, hgen⟩ := exists_affineOpen_nonZeroDivisor I hI x
  exact ⟨V, hxV, f, isRegular_iff_mem_nonZeroDivisors.mpr hf, hgen⟩

/-- **The remark following Stacks Project, Definition 01WR:** an effective Cartier divisor is
locally principal. Immediate from the forward direction of Tag 01WS, forgetting the
nonzerodivisor property of the generator. -/
theorem isLocallyPrincipal (hI : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor I) :
    Stacks.Divisors.IsLocallyPrincipal I := fun x => by
  obtain ⟨V, hxV, f, -, hgen⟩ := exists_affineOpen_nonZeroDivisor I hI x
  exact ⟨V, hxV, ⟨f, by rw [hgen, Ideal.submodule_span_eq]⟩⟩

open _root_.Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CartierComplementDense in
/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 07ZU, density half, unconditionally.** The open complement of the
support of an effective Cartier divisor is scheme-theoretically dense.

`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CartierComplementDense`
`.isSchemeTheoreticallyDense_supportCompl_of_nonZeroDivisor` proves this from the affine-local
nonzerodivisor description, which it carried as a hypothesis because [Stacks, Tag 01WS] was
missing; `exists_affineOpen_nonZeroDivisor` supplies it.

No `@[stacks 07ZU]` attribute is attached: Tag 07ZU has two assertions, and the affineness of
`U ⟶ S` is not proved anywhere in this repository. -/
@[ega "IV 20.2.9" "special case"]
theorem isSchemeTheoreticallyDense_supportCompl
    (hI : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor I) :
    Scheme.Opens.IsSchemeTheoreticallyDense I.support.compl :=
  isSchemeTheoreticallyDense_supportCompl_of_nonZeroDivisor I
    (exists_affineOpen_nonZeroDivisor I hI)

end Stacks.CartierAffineLocal

end
